    "body": "By the way, this can be verified (that the behaviors are as I've described) by looking at the web platform test [/fullscreen/api/document-exit-fullscreen-nested-in-iframe.html](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/fullscreen/api/document-exit-fullscreen-nested-in-iframe.html) (it's not passing on Firefox due to a bug, that I've already submitted a fix for, and unrelated to this issue) - because it would \"exit fully\" on the first `exitFullscreen()`, since the top level document is actually a simple fullscreen document, but the iframe document *isn't*. However, what we observe is that the iframe document first removes the first fullscreen element (and remains in fullscreen, with no resize, since there's still one element in it's top layer that is fullscreen)",
